  "methodology": [
    "Only actual dispatched receipt request hashes are matched using native bodyForReceipt; tokenizer-only candidates are excluded.",
    "Role and schema partitions use stable JSON bytes; serialization framing is the residual, giving exact prompt-byte reconciliation. Wire adds model/provider parameters.",
    "A repeated item is byte-identical to an item in an earlier matched request of the same arm; same-request duplicates alone do not qualify. Repetition resets per trajectory.",
    "Source body UTF-8 bytes are a non-additive submeasure of tool messages; JSON escaping is excluded and source text is never emitted.",
    "Repeated assistant measures exact whole assistant messages, including their tool-call argument serialization. Explicit reasoning field counts disclose sizes only."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Unmatched dispatched requests are excluded from byte attribution, not assumed empty.",
    "Exact repetition misses partially overlapping source ranges and edited messages; no semantic deduplication estimate.",
    "Transport JSON bytes do not equal model input tokens; byte shares imply no token-reduction or safe-deletion claim.",
    "Repeated evidence may be necessary after recycling; removing it can increase rediscovery, output tokens, calls or errors."
